function R = phase5b_registry(varargin)
%PHASE5B_REGISTRY  Device registry v2 study rows + physical presence rows (Phase-5b Tasks C2+C7).
%   R = PHASE5B_REGISTRY() returns struct with fields:
%     .devices    struct array (v1 21 locked fields + physical_CT_ratio,
%                 selected_CT_core, protection_function, study_CT_ratio,
%                 layer in PHYSICAL/STUDY = 26 fields)
%     .ct_primary 15000 (primary protection-report ratio, kept from v1)
%     .ct_legacy  16000 (fenced sensitivity reference only, never substituted
%                 into any device row; 16k scope is generator-CT-only per
%                 phase5b_ct_scope)
%     .gen        v1 gen + Imax_A 14309 (ledger GEN-Imax-14309, pp.6-7)
%     .topology   v1 topology + breaker_52G '10BAC10' + rating_100kA 100
%                 (ledger GCB-10BAC10-100kA)
%
%   C2 scope: the 7 v1 study rows corrected (rows 1-7, byte-preserved).
%   C7 scope: 26 PHYSICAL presence rows appended (rows 8-33, same 26-field
%   schema). Settings carried ONLY where sourced: GEN-51-SIEMENS-BL 17171 A
%   DT-?? USER_ASSERTED_PENDING_DOC (mirrored 1:1 from phase5b_pickup C3);
%   GEN-87G start 0.20 pu USER_ASSERTED_PENDING_DOC + master-S21 Status-C
%   corroboration (0.20 x 12019 = 2403.8 A); GEN-52G 12.4 kA cont / 100 kA
%   breaking SOURCE-BACKED; all other PHYSICAL pickups NaN + TMS/EF NaN
%   (never invented). Trip fields (breaker_ref, and zones trip matrix)
%   stay NOT-DETERMINABLE/empty: 52G vs Q0, 86 lockout, BF paths never
%   inferred.
%
%   Alias map (binding carry-over 2; also implemented callable in
%   phase5b_id_aliases.m for testability):
%     'GEN-51-SI'        -> 'GEN-51'   (canonical STUDY phase OC)
%     'GEN-51N-SI-STUDY' -> 'GEN-51N'  (canonical STUDY earth-fault)
%   Registry keeps canonical v1 IDs GEN-51/GEN-51N (layer STUDY); aliases
%   resolve via phase5b_id_aliases (both ways tested: alias->canonical and
%   canonical idempotent + pickup equality). Baseline GEN-51-SIEMENS-BL is
%   a distinct PHYSICAL row (not an alias).
%   Corrections vs v1 (spec S4, C2 rows 1-7):
%     GSUT-HV-51, GIS-Q0-51, GIS-Q0-50 CT 2000/1-assumed -> 1600/1
%     SOURCE-BACKED (ledger GIS-bay-1600/1 + GSUT-1600/1-cores); GEN CTs
%     15000/1 unchanged; no 2000 or 16000 ratio on any row; study-row TMS
%     0.20 uniform initial (master Status C); pickups stay NaN — GEN-51-SI
%     carries rule tag RULE-1.2xMAXLOAD for recompute by phase5b_pickup in
%     C4 (never hard-coded here). Exact function-core mapping is
%     NOT-DETERMINABLE where bay-dependent (master S18), recorded in
%     selected_CT_core. All rows layer STUDY in C2.
%   All errors 'phase5b'-prefixed (frozen v1 functions keep 'phase5' IDs).
